{"id": "xireland", "name": "The Burren", "short": "The Burren", "place": "County Clare and County Galway", "lat": 53.0, "lon": -9.0, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Ireland", "blurb": "Limestone pavement, winter-grazing cattle and the flowers that grow in its cracks.", "tip": {"id": "cattle", "title": "Take away winter grazing", "text": "Cattle grazed on the uplands each winter keep scrub down. Set Native beef cattle to -100% and watch hazel and the flowers of the short turf."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: The Burren", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Burren"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: European pine marten", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_pine_marten"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Dryas octopetala", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dryas_octopetala"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "The Burren", "icon": "sage", "tier": "overview", "kind": "Grassland", "park": true, "nodes": [{"id": "avens", "sp": "dryas octopetala", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "A small evergreen shrub of limestone outcrops. In the Burren it grows beside Mediterranean plants, a mix of arctic-alpine and southern flora.", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "cranesbill", "sp": "geranium sanguineum", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "trefoil", "sp": "lotus corniculatus", "xh": 0.46, "name": "Bird's-foot-trefoil", "ic": "sage"}, {"id": "thyme", "sp": "thymus praecox", "xh": 0.64}, {"id": "hazel", "sp": "corylus avellana", "xh": 0.84, "name": "Hazel", "desc": "A shrub that spreads as scrub where grazing has declined. Its nuts feed squirrels and small rodents."}, {"id": "cattle", "sp": "bos taurus", "xh": 0.05, "name": "Native beef cattle", "wiki": "Cattle", "desc": "Hardy cattle are traditionally grazed on the uplands from October to April (winterage). This keeps scrub down and the flower-rich turf open.", "badge": "Keystone grazer"}, {"id": "goat", "sp": "capra hircus", "xh": 0.2, "wiki": "Feral goat", "desc": "Free-living goats roam the Burren uplands and browse its plants and shrubs."}, {"id": "rabbit", "sp": "oryctolagus cuniculus", "xh": 0.35, "desc": "A grazer of short turf and an important prey animal for foxes, stoats, badgers and pine martens."}, {"id": "woodmouse", "sp": "apodemus sylvaticus", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "A small seed and fruit eater and prey for almost every predator in the web."}, {"id": "squirrel", "sp": "sciurus vulgaris", "xh": 0.65, "desc": "Eats hazel nuts and seeds. Wikipedia says pine martens help red squirrels by suppressing invasive grey squirrels."}, {"id": "meadowbrown", "sp": "maniola jurtina", "xh": 0.8, "desc": "The most recorded insect in the area. The adult feeds on flower nectar such as thyme."}, {"id": "carder", "sp": "bombus pascuorum", "xh": 0.94}, {"id": "frog", "sp": "rana temporaria", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "An amphibian that eats insects and other small invertebrates. Otters, foxes, badgers and hedgehogs are all recorded eating frogs.", "ic": "snake"}, {"id": "hedgehog", "sp": "erinaceus europaeus", "xh": 0.38}, {"id": "stoat", "sp": "mustela erminea", "xh": 0.6, "desc": "A small mustelid hunter of rabbits, mice and voles."}, {"id": "badger", "sp": "meles meles", "xh": 0.85, "desc": "An omnivore that eats small mammals, frogs and bumblebees among other foods."}, {"id": "marten", "sp": "martes martes", "xh": 0.3, "tl": 4, "desc": "The Burren is one of its strongholds in Ireland. It eats small mammals, frogs, insects, berries and carrion.", "badge": "Keystone predator"}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.7, "tl": 4, "desc": "A generalist predator of rabbits, rodents and frogs that also eats carrion."}, {"id": "limestone", "sp": "limestone pavement", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "atlantic rain", "xh": 0.35}, {"id": "mild", "sp": "mild winters", "xh": 0.6}, 